{
  "dom_id": "step-q110147",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14214993/assets/7b89a8737e3fcb062d5cb53a8832bc3d8f30273696b3be0e8c47d25ba158fa60.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graphs of $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$, where $g(x)=f(x+a)+b.$ What are the values of $a$ and $b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that every point on the graph $y=g(x)$ is three units *to the left* and two units *up* of the corresponding point on the graph of $y=f(x).$ \n\nSo, we conclude that $g(x)=f(x+3)+2,$ and therefore $a=3$ and $b=2.$",
